  "title": "review: Execute and fix-delta prompts commit-first (cherry-pick 11ec80b) with the prompt-pinning tests updated to the new contract",
  "spec": "Why: T-1410 (commit 11ec80b on task/T-1410) rewrote .orchestrator/prompts/execute.md and fix-delta.md as intended (commit first, focused tests in the foreground, never background, the daemon runs the full gate) and added tests/test_instructions.py::test_execute_prompt_commits_before_focused_tests. Its gate went red on four existing tests that pin the old prompt contract:\n- tests/test_spawn.py Render.test_execute_prompt_names_gate_and_commit and Render.test_fix_delta_prompt_names_gate_and_commit assert '.claude/hooks/tests-green.sh' appears in the prompts; the new contract deliberately removes it.\n- tests/test_spawn.py Render.test_templates_with_packet_placeholder_put_rules_before_it pins a hash of the template text.\n- tests/test_executor.py Executor.test_fallback_claude_when_codex_cooling (check whether it pins prompt text too; if it fails for another reason, report it and do not change it).\n\nWhat: start from goal/T-1403, `git cherry-pick 11ec80b`, then update those tests to the new contract: the two names_gate_and_commit tests assert the prompts say to commit before testing, run the acceptance-named tests in the foreground, never background a command, and that the daemon runs the full gate (and that tests-green.sh is NOT named); update the pinned hash to the new template; keep each test's intent. Do not change the prompts beyond 11ec80b unless a test reveals a real gap. Keep every {placeholder}; no double braces.\n\nCommit, then run tests/test_instructions.py, tests/test_spawn.py and tests/test_executor.py in the foreground. Never background a command, never the full gate.",
