    "summary": "Verified against the actual worktree (task/T-1421, HEAD 4859ede) rather than assuming from the diff text alone. Both .orchestrator/prompts/execute.md and fix-delta.md now say to commit before testing, run only acceptance-named tests in the foreground, never background, note the 10-minute limit, and state the daemon runs the full gate; neither names .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh. Ran tests/test_instructions.py, tests/test_spawn.py, tests/test_executor.py directly with unittest: test_execute_prompt_commits_before_focused_tests, test_execute_prompt_names_gate_and_commit, test_fix_delta_prompt_names_gate_and_commit, test_templates_with_packet_placeholder_put_rules_before_it (updated hash), and test_fallback_claude_when_codex_cooling all pass. Two unrelated errors appear in test_spawn.py (test_packet_prior_worker_section_lists_partial_facts, test_prior_worker_section_inert_in_shadow_mode) due to a missing 'goal/G' git ref in the temp test repo; confirmed these fail identically on HEAD~1 (pre-task-1421 commit) too, so they're a pre-existing environment issue outside this diff's scope, not a regression introduced here. Changed files match the scope list exactly (execute.md, fix-delta.md, test_instructions.py, test_spawn.py, test_executor.py). Acceptance criteria satisfied.",
